      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`Internlm2ToolParser.extract_tool_calls_streaming` splits the accumulated text on the tool-call marker with an unbounded `str.split` and unpacks the result into exactly two values:\n\n```python\nnew_delta = current_text[last_pos:]\ntext, action = new_delta.split(\"<|action_start|><|plugin|>\")\n```\n\n`self.position` is only advanced past text that precedes the first marker, and `self.current_tool_id` never exceeds `0`, so the `if self.current_tool_id > 0` early-return never fires on the tool-call path. Once the model streams a **second** `<|action_start|><|plugin|>` block, `current_text[last_pos:]` contains two markers, `split` returns three parts, and the unpack raises:\n\n```\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)\n```\n\nThis line runs **before** the method's `try/except` (which starts a few lines later), so the exception propagates and aborts the streaming request rather than being swallowed.\n\n## Trigger\n\nA model emitting two consecutive tool-call blocks, e.g. accumulated text:\n\n```\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>{\"name\": \"f\", \"parameters\": {}}<|action_end|><|action_start|><|plugin|>{\"name\": \"g\", \"parameters\": {}}<|action_end|>\n```\n\nInternLM2 is documented as not supporting parallel tool calls, but that is a limitation, not a guard — nothing constrains the decoder from emitting a second block, and a misprompted/hallucinating model realistically can.\n\n## Fix\n\nSplit only on the first marker with `str.partition`:\n\n```python\ntext, _, action = new_delta.partition(\"<|action_start|><|plugin|>\")\n```\n\nThe subsequent `action.split(\"<|action_end|>\")[0]` already isolates the first tool call, so single-tool-call behavior is unchanged. Verified that for single-block input the extracted `(text, action)` is identical to the old code.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded `test_streaming_two_action_blocks_no_unpack_error` in `tests/tool_parsers/test_internlm2_tool_parser.py`, which streams two action blocks and asserts the extractor does not raise. It fails on `main` (ValueError) and passes with this change.\n\n```\npytest tests/tool_parsers/test_internlm2_tool_parser.py -k two_action_blocks\n```",
